"OverallSummary": "This case involves violations by SpeedTrader, Inc. related to best execution, AML compliance, and Form CRS disclosures, but does not include Care Obligation violations under Regulation Best Interest. The firm failed to meet its best execution obligations under FINRA Rule 5310 by not considering all relevant execution quality factors and not comparing execution quality of existing routing arrangements to other markets. From January 2017 to July 2022, SpeedTrader improperly interjected third parties between itself and the best market for securities. The firm also had inadequate supervisory systems and procedures for best execution and AML compliance. SpeedTrader failed to monitor suspicious trading activity, particularly by certain foreign customers who traded low-priced securities and generated significant losses. Additionally, the firm made false statements on its Form CRS regarding disciplinary history. Due to the firm's financial condition, FINRA imposed no monetary fine but required SpeedTrader to retain an independent consultant to review and remediate its supervisory systems and procedures. The violations did not involve making unsuitable recommendations to customers, as SpeedTrader primarily provided self-directed online brokerage services to approximately 850 retail customers."
